# ── About window (\n = line break) ─────────────────────────────────────
INFO_WND_TITLE=About — MyPuppyD
INFO_TAGLINE=ECU identification and tuning engine
INFO_SEC_ABOUT=About the application
INFO_ABOUT=MyPuppyD identifies the controller from the BIN file alone and locates the maps inside it — no A2L files, no hunting for addresses by hand.\nMap patterns are stored per ECU family, so recognition can be extended without rebuilding the program.\nMaps open as a grid, a 2D chart or in 3D; you edit them and save them as a project version — with change history and checksum control.\nThe Lopper tab adds ready service solutions (DPF, EGR, DTC, AdBlue and others) for the recognised controller.
INFO_SEC_LIC=Licence
INFO_HWID=HWID:
INFO_LIC_STATUS=License status:
INFO_VALID_UNTIL=Valid until:
INFO_DAYS=days
INFO_SEC_TUTORIAL=Quick start
INFO_BTN_PREV=◄ Back
INFO_BTN_NEXT=Next ►
INFO_BTN_CLOSE=Close
INFO_SHORTCUT=Keyboard shortcut:
INFO_TUT1_TITLE=1. Main — load a file
INFO_TUT1_TEXT="Import" loads a BIN file and creates a project for it; "Export" saves the current version.\nThe project version list takes you back to any saved state — "Rename" and "Version description" let you label them.
INFO_TUT1_M1=Import / export a BIN file
INFO_TUT1_M2=Recently opened projects — double-click to open
INFO_TUT1_M3=Modification history of the current version
INFO_TUT2_TITLE=2. Maps — browse and edit
INFO_TUT2_TEXT=Pick a map from the list on the left. The "View" list switches grid, 2D chart and 3D; "Rotate view" turns the grid.\nRight-click the grid for the edit menu, Ctrl+click to select several cells — the full editor shortcut list is under the gear → "Supported".
INFO_TUT2_M1=Preview mode: grid / chart / 3D
INFO_TUT2_M2=List of detected maps
INFO_TUT2_M3=Options: data type, change highlighting, list view
INFO_TUT3_TITLE=3. Learning / Detection
INFO_TUT3_TEXT="Detection" looks for maps in a file, "Learning" adds new patterns from a file+CSV pair, "Database" shows the pattern store.\nPick the BIN file with the "…" button on the right and press "Detect" — progress and result go to the terminal below.
INFO_TUT3_M1=Mode: Detection / Learning / Database
INFO_TUT3_M2=Pick the BIN file with the "…" button
INFO_TUT3_M3="Detect" starts the detection run
INFO_TUT4_TITLE=4. Lopper — solutions
INFO_TUT4_TEXT=Lopper recognises the controller from the loaded file and enables the switches for the solutions available to it.\nThe full matrix of supported controllers — including the "Map scaner" column — lives under the gear, in the "Solutions..." menu.
INFO_TUT4_M1=Vehicle brand and model selection
INFO_TUT4_M2=Solutions available for the controller
INFO_TUT4_M3=DTC codes read out

