MECH_HINT_VMAX=1. Flash the file (bench/OBD) and check that no new fault codes appear.\n2. Limiter OFF: closed track or roller dyno — no cut-off at the former limit (e.g. 250 km/h); only rpm/gearing limits.\n3. New speed X km/h: smooth torque limitation at X km/h by GPS (the speedometer usually reads a few % high).\n4. Check cruise control/ACC and that there are no DSC warnings.
MECH_HINT_COOLTGT=1. Flash the file and check that no new fault codes appear (thermostat, fan, coolant sensor).\n2. Warm up the engine: in live data the coolant temperature should settle at the new target (idle and steady driving, a few minutes).\n3. Fan: at the temperatures from the map the fan speed should match the new values; also check fan after-run after engine shut-off.\n4. Watch the temperature gauge — a target set too low may set a thermostat fault.
MECH_HINT_EGTMON=1. Flash the file and check the fault code list — disabled exhaust temperature sensor codes should not appear.\n2. Live data: exhaust temperature sensor readings unchanged (only thresholds and ECU reactions are changed).\n3. Dyno, full load: power should not drop while the turbine inlet temperature stays below the new threshold; monitor it with an external EGT probe.\n4. Higher thresholds mean higher risk of turbocharger and catalyst damage — do not exceed the turbo manufacturer limits.
